{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Now the Amalekite and the Canaanite, etc.</b> The intent of this notification here, and also the addition of the vav, is because HaShem had decreed that the entire generation would not enter the land and would die in the wilderness, yet He said that He would not kill them all at once — as one man — and therefore they needed to tarry in the wilderness a long time, as He in fact disclosed in the ensuing verses. Now there is a side to say that they would dwell in that place the entire time; therefore He said <b>now the Amalekite</b>, etc. — meaning, they are unable to tarry in this place, for you are liable to fall before them. This is along the lines of their saying (Tanhuma, Vayigash 1): the prosecuting angel [= Satan] denounces in the hour of danger. Therefore <b>tomorrow turn</b>, etc. And even though we find that they dwelt afterward there many days, as it is written (Deuteronomy 1:46): ״וַתֵּשְׁבוּ בְקָדֵשׁ יָמִים רַבִּים״, and they of blessed memory said (Seder Olam): nineteen years — that was upon their return, by which time the sin had already been contracted and diminished, unlike before. And by this we find a reason why they did not then tarry there as they tarried afterward. And the reason He said <b>now the Amalekite</b> with the addition of a vav is to link the matter with the beginning of the utterance of ״if they see״, etc., for He further adds the decree of the journeys, as He says ״tomorrow turn״ — the vav being drawn along with the statement ״tomorrow turn.״"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:21.675731251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}